forget about fantastic beasts this time  around we're trying to find fantastic  reviews and they're harder to come by  than you might think correct three  points to hufflepuff fantastic beasts  the secrets of dumbledore is the third  film in the wizarding world prequel  series directed by harry potter veteran  david yates it picks up several years  after the events of 2018's fantastic  feasts the crimes of grindelwald the new  installment follows professor albus  dumbledore as he enlists magiszuologist  newt scamander to help him fight against  gellert grindelwald the dark wizard  seeking out control of the wizarding  world jk rowling who wrote the first two  films returned as a screenwriter  although this time she teamed up with  steve cloves aka the writer of all but  one of the harry potter films the harry  potter series is one of the most  successful franchises of all time but  the fantastic beasts movie spin-offs  haven't quite seen the same success with  audiences or critics the first film in  the prequel series 2016's fantastic  beasts and where to find them fared  pretty well with its reviews earning  itself a 74 score on rotten tomatoes  however the follow-up film fantastic  beasts the crimes of grindelwald didn't  even come close to achieving the same  kind of success with viewers widely  derided for its overstuffed screenplay  it holds a rotten tomatoes rating of  just 36 percent  so how does the upcoming secrets of  dumbledore compare to its predecessors  when it comes to critical consensus well  as of the making of this video it falls  squarely in the middle at a 62 score on  the tomato meter some reviews are okay  with it and some really aren't here's a  rundown of what these divided critics  think things are not quite what they  appear  despite the secrets of dumbledore  nabbing a better tomato meter score than  its 2018 predecessor many critics were  still not impressed with the latest  effort of the franchise speaking for  many of the critics who didn't love the  film entertainment weekly declared that  the third time is not quite the charm  some critics found that the film lacked  focus and felt generally all over the  place one of the critics kate urbland of  indy wire wrote that the film offers an  unwieldy mostly unsettling mashup of  adult themes and childish whimsy made  still more inscrutable by too many  subplots too many characters and a tone  that fears wildly off course at every  possible turn  meanwhile charles bramasko of polygon  first suggests the series should have  called it quits after the last movie  before pointing out that newt who began  the series as the protagonist is barely  involved in what's become the actual  plot of this series he wrote  newt's convoluted anticlimactic quest to  secure and deliver his precious cargo  lacks the delighted curiosity that lent  the first fantastic beasts a much-needed  bump in charm finally in a scathing  review siddhant adlaka of ign wrote  there are two more entries planned but  ending the harry potter spin-off here  would be a mercy there's nothing  fantastic about the new movie the story  is dull the characters are duller  it's not all bad though though the  review for entertainment weekly implied  the film missed the mark overall writer  leah greenblatt still found some merit  to the movie she concluded her review on  the note that the secrets of dumbledore  is a major step up from its predecessor  deeming it quote nimbler and sweeter and  more cohesive in its storyline  greenblatt also noted that this time  around the cast are given more room to  explore the stakes their characters face  instead of just shuttling along from  scene to scene on the subject of the  acting peter de bruges of variety noted  that mass mickelson is better suited for  the character of gellert grindelwald  than johnny depp who played the  character in the previous film de bruges  wrote that mikkelsen comes off favorably  as a more grounded less cartoonishly  menacing version of the character he  also gave credit to the screenplay which  he found far more focused and easier to  follow than the last one in one of the  most positive reviews four out of five  stars linda merrick of the jewish  chronicle called it a welcome return to  form and gave special praise to the  performances of law and mickelson she  summed up the movie by saying gates  rolling in cloves have given us an  engaging story peppered throughout with  some funny heartfelt and exciting action  sequences what side of the divide will  you be on the only way to find out is to  see the movie for yourself when  fantastic beasts the secrets of  dumbledore premieres in theaters on  april 15th who wouldn't like our chances  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies and tv shows are  coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]
 

